---
import TesterLayout from "@/layouts/TesterLayout.astro";
import { LeftNavi } from "vue-editors";
import { navItems } from "@/data";

const currentPath = Astro.url.pathname;

const sample1 =
      (`<div style="width: 100%; height: 150px;">
      <!-- Set the size of parent container. Editor takes 100% of height and width. -->
      <qrtl-editor type="monaco" lang="javascript" code="console.log('Hello, world!');"></qrtl-editor>
</div>

<!-- Load the component at the end of the page. -->
<` +
      `script type="module" src="https://code.quartal.com/qrtl-editor.js"></` +
      `script>`);

---

<script type="module" src="/qrtl-editor.js"></script>
<TesterLayout title="Quartal Hub, Code UI">
  <div class="container" style="max-height: calc(100vh - 220px); overflow-y: auto;">
    <p class="lead">
      Provides a set of code editors for Quartal Hub. These editors are
      typically used as embedded in Quartal Hub user interfaces as well as
      external UIs that utilize Quartal Hub components.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-3">
        <LeftNavi navItems={navItems} currentPath={currentPath} />
      </div>
      <div class="col-9">
        <h1>Usage</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          All the code editors are available through <strong
            ><code>qrtl-editor</code></strong
          > component. The component is a <a
            href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/is"
            target="_blank">custom element</a
          >.<br />
          As such it can be used in any HTML page and in any framework.
        </p>
        <div style="width: 100%; height: 150px;">
          <qrtl-editor type="monaco" id="previewEditor" lang="html" code={sample1}></qrtl-editor>
        </div>
        ...renders as:
        <div style="width: 100%; height: 150px;">
          <qrtl-editor
            type="monaco"
            lang="javascript"
            code="console.log('Hello, world!');"></qrtl-editor>
        </div>
        <h2 class="mt-3">Attributes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>type</code> - Type of the editor to show. Can be <code
              >monaco</code
            >, <code>monaco-react</code>, <code>expression</code>, <code
              >function</code
            >, <code>class</code>, <code>files</code>, <code>excalidraw</code
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>view</code> - Optional view style for editors (for example, expression
            editor <code>plain</code> or <code>excel</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>read-only</code> - If present, editor is read-only.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>lang</code> - Language of the code to show in the editor. Used together
            with code in single-file usecases.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>code</code> - Code to show in the editor. Used in simple single-file
            usecases.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>url</code> - URL of the code to show in the editor. Alternative
            to code. URL must support anonymous access.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>data</code> - Full data to pass to the editor. Used in complex usecases.
            Each editor type defines its own data structure as an interface.
          </li>
          <li>
            <code>change</code> - Event that is triggered when the code changes.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <h2 class="mt-3">URL based usage</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          There is a separate component <code>qrtl-editor-url</code> that can be used to load code from a URL.
          This is useful for loading code from a remote source, such as a GitHub repository.
        </p>
        <p>The component has the following attributes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>url</code> - URL of the code to show in the editor.</li>
          <li><code>type</code> - Type of the editor to show. See above for possible values.</li>
          <li><code>lang</code> - Optional possibility to force the language of the code to show in the editor.
            Typically, the language is detected automatically from the URL.
          </li>          
          <li><code>view</code> - Optional view style for editors.</li>
          <li><code>editable</code> - If present, editor is editable. Default is read-only.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 class="mt-3">Use directly as pages</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          The <code>qrtl-editor</code> component is essentially just an iframe that loads the code editor.
          As such, you can also access the editors directly as pages:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/monaco" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/monaco</a> - Monaco editor</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/monaco-react" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/monaco-react</a> - Monaco editor (React version)</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/markdown" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/markdown</a> - Markdown editor (WYSIWYG)</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/markdown-hybrid" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/markdown-hybrid</a> - Markdown editor (hybrid, Obsidian-like): for test / evaluation purposes only, use the main Markdown editor (<code>/markdown</code>) instead</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/expression" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/expression</a> - Expression editor</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/function" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/function</a> - Function editor</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/class" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/class</a> - Class editor</li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/files" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/files</a> - Files editor (many files). No <code>code</code> or <code>url</code> parameter: the host sends the files with messages, see the <a href="./files/demo">demo</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://code.quartal.com/excalidraw" target="_blank">https://code.quartal.com/excalidraw</a> - Excalidraw editor</li>
        </ul>
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</TesterLayout>
